• Participants with metaiodobenzylguanidine (MIBG)-avid neuroblastoma must also undergo MIBG scintigraphy in addition to CT/MRI as above.""" .

    e:t02-r013-c003 a st:SourceCell ;
        st:column e:t02-c003 ;
        st:row e:t02-r013 ;
        st:value "• Participants in brain tumor-related cohorts and those with a history of brain metastasis or symptoms should undergo MRI of the brain without and with contrast every 9 weeks (± 7 days) from start of treatment up to 54 weeks, and then approximately every 12 weeks (± 7 days), or sooner if clinically indicated. Tumor assessment schedule should be maintained regardless of dose delays. Cerebrospinal fluid (CSF), if clinically indicated, should be followed as per Response Assessment in Pediatric Neuro-Oncology guidelines." .

