        st:value "• Participants in brain tumor-related cohorts and those with a history of brain metastasis or symptoms should undergo MRI of the brain without and with contrast every 9 weeks (± 7 days) from start of treatment up to 54 weeks, and then approximately every 12 weeks (± 7 days), or sooner if clinically indicated until disease progression (including treatment beyond progression) or end of study, whichever occurs later. Cerebrospinal fluid (CSF), if clinically indicated, should be followed as per Response Assessment in Pediatric Neuro-Oncology guidelines." .

    e:t03-r014-c005 a st:SourceCell ;
